<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polish–Soviet War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a>–<a href="/years/1921">1921</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Polish–Bolshevik War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Polish–Soviet War was fought from 1919 to 1921 between the Second Polish Republic and Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> over the lands between them. After Polish forces took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a> in 1920, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> advanced to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jozef-pilsudski">Józef Piłsudski</a>'s counter-offensive won the Battle of Warsaw; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-riga">Peace of Riga</a> (1921) divided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a> and Ukraine between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and the Soviet republics.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polish-soviet-war.jpg" alt="Polish–Soviet War" width="320" height="566" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: nieznani · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Polish-soviet_war_montage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
